        "nobel_worthiness": "Quantum key distribution gave quantum information a clear operational consequence: communication security grounded in physical principles, with lasting influence on quantum technologies.",
        "attribution": "Bennett and Brassard introduced the influential BB84 protocol; Ekert independently introduced an entanglement-based approach that clarified deep links to Bell tests.",
        "maturity": "The foundational ideas are mature and have been experimentally demonstrated, while deployment and practical security remain active engineering questions.",
        "uncertainties": [
